                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              to the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+categories"} cartesian closed categories
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
              preserving the CC structure.
            %li
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representing object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in K
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(-,U) \cong P_0
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mn 0
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mi o
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_0 : K^o \to Set
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
              of objects of the corresponding CCC.
            %li
              Such that for any
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta \in K
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(\pi) \colon P(\Delta) \to P(\Delta \times U)
              induced from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi \colon \Delta \times U \to \Delta
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∀
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall \colon P(\Delta \times U) \to P(\Delta)
              satisfying a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck-Chevalley+condition"} Beck-Chevalley condition
          %p
            Typically, the objects of the category of
            %em kinds
            are restricted to be generated by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} products
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          %p
            Note that this models the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mi η
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta\eta
            equivalence of System F only, not the more complex notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                relational parametricity
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/relational+parametricity"} ?
            %em relationally parametric model
            of System F is
          %ol
            %li
              A model of System F
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal"} internal
              to the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflexive+graphs"} reflexive graphs
            %li
              Such that the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s,t) : P_e(\Delta_e) \to P_v(s(\Delta_e)) \times P_v(t(\Delta_e))
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration"} fibration
          %p
            Note that by taking the “vertex” component of such a model, we get an underlying ordinary “equational” model of System F, and so we can see a relatonally parametric model as an extension of an equational model. The internalization to reflexive graphs models the relational structures: the “edge” components are the relations, the source/target maps ensure that each relation lies over an ordinary structure, and the reflexive edge models the notion of an identity/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equality
            relation. The fibration requirement then provides a rich supply of relations: given a relation R and morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi s
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mi s
                  %mo →
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_s : B_s \to s(R)
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi t
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi t
                    %mo →
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_t : B_t \to t(R)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi s
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R[f_s,f_t]
            with source and target
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi s
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_s,B_t
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is an identity relation and one of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi s
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_s,f_t
            is the identity, this is a kind of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+of+a+function"} graph relation
            of a morphism. Compare the definition of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/virtual+equipment"} virtual equipment
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+variable"} type variable
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory+with+type+variables"} dependent type theory with type variables
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The calculus now called
            %em System F
            was developed independently in the following works:
          %ul
            %li#Girard72
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Yves+Girard"}> Jean-Yves Girard
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Interprétation functionelle et élimination des coupures dans l’arithmétique d’ordre supérieure
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.cs.cmu.edu/afs/cs.cmu.edu/user/kw/www/scans/girard72thesis.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Girard-InterpretationFunctionelle.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+C.+Reynolds"}> John C. Reynolds
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Towards a theory of type structure
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-06859-7_148"} doi
          %p The hyperdoctrine-like notion of model:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R.A.G.+Seely"}> R.A.G. Seely
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Categorical Semantics for Higher Order Polymorphic Lambda Calculus
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/2273831"} doi
          %p The reflexive graph/fibrational view of parametricity:
          %ul
            %li
              Brian Dunphy and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Uday+Reddy"} Uday Reddy
              = succeed "," do
                %em Parametric Limits
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1109/LICS.2004.1319618"} doi
